Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:11:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] Runner: the players' tags through the relay

Each runner announces its seats' tags after HELLO (TAG <seat> <tag>: SRNP_TAG for its first seat, else
SRNP_TAGS' entry); the relay keeps them and sends TAGS <tag 0>,<tag 1>,... to every connection at each
new one and to each newcomer; the runner takes them (SetSeatTag) over SRNP_TAGS'. The tags change while
the runner runs: they are a versioned array, and the textures (labels, results) are drawn again at each
new version; the waiting screen reads them as they come. Only shown: measured with 3 runners each
knowing only its own tag, every tag on every screen (waiting screen, labels, results), 98 checksums
equal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
