 //   HELLO <seat> <seats> <delay>     delay: the first <delay> frames have no inputs (neutral)
 //   IN <frame> <seat> <pad>          pad: 16 hex digits (below)
 //   CK <frame> <seat> <hash>         hash: 16 hex digits (FNV-1a 64 of the game's state)
+//   TAG <seat> <tag>                 the seat's player tag (up to 8 characters, no space or comma)
 // relay -> client
 //   WAIT <present> <seats> <states>  at each arrival and every 2 s until no seat is expected; one
 //                                    letter a seat: O expected, V there, X left before the start
 //   GO [<seat>:<character>/<gear>]   the runners leave their first frame; each seat that left is the
 //                                    AI's, with a character the relay drew at random
 //   OF <frame> <pad seat 0> <pad seat 1> ...
+//   TAGS <tag 0>,<tag 1>,...         the tags the relay knows ("-": none), at each new one and to
+//                                    each newcomer; only shown (labels, results, waiting screen)
 // A pad is 8 bytes: buttons (16 bits: A B X Y Z Start Up Down Left Right L R), main stick X, Y,
 // C-stick X, Y (signed, -127..127), L, R (0..255).
 #if defined(_WIN32)
@@ -25,6 +28,7 @@
